    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          1
        ],
        "content": "## Analyze customer feedback from Zendesk and Gong with Claude and report in Notion\n\nProduct and success teams that read tickets one at a time and miss the pattern.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: Daily pulls from each source; the weekly report compiles Monday morning.\n1. Collect feedback\n2. Classify by theme and sentiment\n3. Extract the quotable line\n4. Aggregate\n5. Write the weekly report\n6. Route urgent items\n7. Deliver and store\n8. Maintain the taxonomy\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Zendesk / Intercom / Gong, Notion + Google Sheets.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the theme taxonomy and the report cadence in the Config node; add Intercom or survey tools as sources.\nGuardrail to keep: Personal data is stripped from quotes; sources are linked, not reproduced.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/customer-feedback-analysis/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}